+# Experimental p3s matrix5 cohort
+
+This personal SM-G998B port selects `uname-5.15.206-bpf-bind-enforcing-matrix5-a17`.
+Actual kernel version remains Linux 5.4.304. This is not a Linux 5.15 upgrade.
+Always-enforcing SELinux, strict CFI and shadow call stack are enabled; the
+FCM5 fragment follows the optional Droidspaces fragment so SYSVIPC stays off.
+DEBUG_LIST and SCHED_DEBUG are enabled. Forced module unloading, debugfs and
+zsmalloc statistics are disabled. The resolved configuration is pinned to
+`fddd29aedb9eaeb3afd8f679f7d0ffb38ad24d10acd094aa5401b0b0d50023a3`.
+
+Build with `EXTRA_CONFIG_FRAGMENTS=unica.config` and
+`FINAL_CONFIG_FRAGMENTS=p3s_matrix.config` using the retained pinned compiler
+and build environment. Patch 0004 supplies CFI-compatible split LTO units,
+the Samsung EMS scheduler-key export, and actual build-config embedding.
+The publisher verifies the embedded config against the resolved build .config.
+Source, compiler, exact-config, ELF/module ABI and image checks remain active.
+Earlier published cohorts are separate and cannot satisfy this profile.
+
+The p3s target preserves the target FBE contract. Host checks do not establish
+policy loading, data migration or successful device boot. Do not install a
+kernel alone into the running ROM; the ROM needs its matched r54 module cohort.
+The current packaging recipe retains the upstream boot-header metadata values;
+final OS/security metadata and encrypted-data behavior require explicit review.
+
+The following sections describe historical upstream provisioning and are not
+proof that this new cohort has completed compilation, publication or boot.
+
 # Retained Floppy/r54 build cohort
 
 The earlier kernel-only repair recommendation is withdrawn as an explanation
